  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the probability of the maximum outcome—25% for A (3000€) and 20% for B (4000€)—and prefers the lower one (B). However, the individual in the verbal report focuses on the probability of winning *any positive amount*, which in both lotteries equals the probability of the non-zero outcome (25% for A, 20% for B). Although numerically the same as the probability of the maximum outcome in this case (since each lottery has only one positive outcome), the conceptual focus differs: the individual emphasizes the chance of avoiding zero, not the likelihood of achieving the maximum. Moreover, the individual prefers Lottery A for its higher chance of a positive outcome, which contradicts the decision reason that would prefer B (lower probability of max outcome). The justification in the report is thus aligned with a 'maximize chance of non-zero gain' heuristic, not the 'prefer lower probability of maximum outcome' rule. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

